TITLE: YGGDRASIL A49+ CONDITIONAL MACRO-LINEAGE HYPOTHESES
DATE: 2026-09-22
STATUS: NON-BINDING FUTURE-LINEAGE NOTE / NOT PREREGISTRATION
ACTIVE EXPERIMENT: A49 / T10A
A49 CREEP AMENDMENT: 60c2b474ea0c9b178f457f95bad6045ef82fbdae
BRANCH: dg1a-ar

PURPOSE

Record conditional successor hypotheses
without contaminating A49.

No A50+ mechanism,
parameter,
arm,
delay,
gain,
or composition
is authorized by this note.

A49 remains
the sole active macro experiment.

CURRENT LAYERING

The research lineage now separates:

1. cell persistence;

2. recovery / refractory plasticity;

3. periphery / spatial population control.

Persistence has useful validated mechanisms.

Recovery has been classified by A48
as a reproducible moderate aid
and is parked.

A49 tests whether
the surviving A45 cooperative core
can control surrounding periphery turnover
during repeated challenge.

A49 SUCCESS INTERPRETATION

If A49 produces:

macro information gain;

safety-clean push-pull behavior;

and nonnegative cycle-to-cycle
challenge-onset core trend,

then the current tested
macro-organization phenotype
has a credible solution.

This does NOT by itself establish
that the full Yggdrasil lineage
is complete.

Later robustness,
scale,
generalization,
novel forcing,
and composition tests
would still be needed.

COMBINED-ONLY HYPOTHESIS

If:

CH_OCC_EXCLUSION alone
does not solve the macro phenotype;

CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY alone
does not solve it;

but CH_PUSH_PULL does;

then the working hypothesis is
a net-flow interaction.

Conceptually:

opposing rebuild pressure
is reduced

while

same-side recruitment flow
is increased.

The combined mechanism
may cross a population-flow boundary
that neither single mechanism
crosses independently.

A49 itself tests
combined-only rescue
without fitting
a continuous strength surface.

POSSIBLE A50 — PUSH/PULL RESPONSE SURFACE

Authorize only if A49 first shows
genuine push-pull macro information gain
and at least one push-pull-only rescue.

A later experiment may map
a preregistered 2-D response surface:

exclusion strength

x

recruitment strength.

Purpose:

identify whether there is
a low-cost region
where weaker exclusion
or weaker recruitment
still preserves the macro effect.

The sweep must be preregistered
before outcomes.

Do not infer a minimum E:R ratio
from A49 alone.

RECOVERY + MACRO SYNERGY HYPOTHESIS

A48 established G5_FULL
as a reproducible moderate
optional recovery aid.

A49 intentionally excludes it.

If A49 alone shows
partial macro improvement
but not full qualification,
a later factorial composition may test:

A45 substrate only;

A45 + frozen G5_FULL;

A49 macro mechanism only;

A49 macro mechanism + frozen G5_FULL.

The scientific question:

does faster post-disturbance recovery
raise the next-cycle core baseline enough
to strengthen periphery control
without changing the periphery rule itself?

No recovery retuning
is allowed inside that composition.

A positive interaction would support
layer synergy:

recovery raises the available core;

periphery control uses that larger core
to alter surrounding population flow.

PHASE-OFFSET / DELAY HYPOTHESIS

Consider only if A49 demonstrates
that amplitude/topology interventions
are insufficient.

Possible evidence pattern:

challenge fields are locally active;

periphery recruitment is measurably altered;

core size is not catastrophically eroding;

yet the population remains
locked to the repeated forcing pattern.

That would justify asking
whether response phase
rather than response amplitude
is the remaining bottleneck.

A future phase-offset experiment
must NOT assume in advance
that the 5:3 phenotype is
a Kuramoto-like entrainment phenomenon.

That is a hypothesis to test.

DELAY SEMANTICS

A true fixed response delay
requires state.

At minimum,
the experiment must specify:

what variable is delayed:

raw local evidence;

signed B update;

committed-state decision;

or defection action;

how many epochs are buffered;

what happens before the buffer fills;

whether recruitment also reads
delayed or current state;

how reversal is handled;

how anti-oracle integrity is proven.

Different delayed variables
are different causal mechanisms.

They must not be conflated.

DELAY GRID

No T/4 to T/3 sweet spot
is frozen by analogy.

If authorized later,
choose a small discrete
preregistered delay set
relative to the actual forcing schedule.

Include:

zero-delay control;

small delay;

intermediate delay;

and at least one delay
large enough to expose anti-phase failure risk.

The purpose is
to measure the response surface,
not confirm a presumed sweet spot.

CIRCADIAN / KURAMOTO ANALOGY

Circadian phase response
and forced-oscillator intuition
may motivate the experiment.

They do not establish
that the software-cell system
shares the same governing dynamics.

Biological and oscillator analogies
remain explanatory,
not proof.

CREEP CONNECTION

Any apparent oscillator suppression
under a future phase-offset mechanism
must retain the A49 creep diagnostic.

A delayed core
that stops flipping
but loses challenge-onset mass
cycle by cycle
is metastable,
not solved.

PLAIN-SPEAK SUMMARY

There are three clean branches
after A49.

If push and pull work together:

map how little of each
we actually need.

If push-pull almost works
and faster recovery
would give it a larger core:

test the frozen recovery aid
as an independent partner.

If spatial control is clearly active
but the population still moves
in lockstep with the forcing:

then test whether
the timing of the response itself
is the problem.

Do not mix those questions
inside A49.

First let A49 tell us
which branch is justified.

